			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2027768">
									

<p>It might be that might threshold for what constitutes purple is wonky and off, but I feel so long as the language is being used&#8230;precisely (?) effectively (?) enough, then it's not purple for me. I felt that the language very much fit the portrayal of the O5 Council-ancient, frightened cabal. I'll also say that &quot;revelations about the true nature of death&quot; are not really my cup of tea, but I feel it was executed well. Honestly, I was expecting some sort of &quot;death is nothingness oh nooooo&quot; revelation, but the actual revelation-damn. The imagery worked for me.</p>
<p>I'm a huge fan of the format screw, if only that it proves that you can really do whatever the fuck you want in an article. For me, a mainlist article is &quot;anything you would get by trying to access a dossier briefing on an SCP object from the Foundation database.&quot; And this&#8230;is it, I guess :p.</p>
<p>+1</p>

