<p>*clap* *clap* *clap*</p>
<p>I was ready to downvote the hell out of this and come rip it apart in the comments until I got to the actual recording. Was where this was headed predictable? Maybe. I figured that the dead guy's experiences were deeply unpleasant. But to me, that didn't matter. This was some old-school, nice creepy shit. This is one of my new favorites.</p>
<p>As to some of the above commentary, all I can say is that people on this site have upvoted more pointless format-screws and <em>far</em> more melodramatic stories than this one. There are occasions where weird formatting and dramatic dialogue work, and that's when there's an actual <em>reason</em> for them. In my opinion, if you're going to write a &quot;this is the afterlife&quot; skip, that's a decent reason.</p>
<p>Upvoted enthusiastically, and my compliments, Atreus.</p>
<p>EDIT: Also, the guy running <em>into</em> 106's chamber. In a lesser article, I would have burst a blood vessel from rolling my eyes so hard. In this one? God <em>damn</em>, dude.</p>

