<p>I went and downvoted that article, partially because of its implications about the O5s, but mostly because it's just a straightforward fountain of youth, which is really boring.</p>
<p>Anyway, I doubt many people still consider those implications to be a part of SCP canon. It seems like one of those goofy elements left over from the early days of the site, back when half the people in the Foundation seemed to be anomalous in some way or other. The vast majority of SCPs and tales that I've read (for instance, SCP-2950) have indicated that the O5s are simply normal humans who are replaced when they step down, retire, or die.</p>

